    "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/THE-BU1LD/NeuroCAD/zipball/v0.5.0a6",
    "body": "NeuroCAD v0.5.0a6 is a bounded public alpha for dimensioned prompt-to-OpenSCAD workflows, editable electronics enclosures, and independently checkable artifact bundles.\n\n- Validated typed project revisions; invalid edits, stale revision evidence, output collisions and bundle tampering fail closed.\n- OpenSCAD/STL generation and compiled enclosure verification, plus browser workbench acceptance in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit.\n- Analytical physics tools use explicit idealized models. Optional exact-CAD and Gmsh integrations retain separate dependency and verification contracts.\n\nDownload the wheel or source distribution together with SHA256SUMS and RELEASE_PROVENANCE.json. Verify the checksums before installing. The provenance receipt records the exact tag, source commit, environment and artifact hashes. See docs/QUICKSTART.md in the tagged source for installation.\n\nRelease acceptance covers the supported Python/platform matrix, fresh wheel and source installations, reproducible builds, the public installer, and compiled enclosure edits/verification. The public download checks run without GitHub credentials; persistent OS service setup is outside that installation receipt.\n\nThis alpha does not establish independent scientific replication, physical fit, human usability, manufacturing suitability or safety. The original compiler study remains terminal mixed; the separate Physics v2 controlled result and Physics v3 engineering status are unchanged. Review generated parts before fabrication.\n"
